From caadb81cdfc0df61ee7e4d6eea4a6ad2b3c75975 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pavel Artsishevsky <polter.rnd@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:00:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: add GTK4 editor UI

Based on tigro's Fedora patch. The GTK4 editor could not load the
GTK3 Glade dialog (GtkDialog.type-hint etc.), which left
gnome-control-center with a broken editor.

- Add a GTK4 dialog UI and separate GResource bundle, including the
  AmneziaWG 3.1 frame, with an aligned grid layout and collapsible
  obfuscation / 3.1 sections
- Pick the GTK3 or GTK4 editor library at runtime
- Use a GtkListBox for the peer list and a GtkRevealer for errors in
  GTK4 builds
- Use the GtkCheckButton API for check boxes under GTK4 (it is no
  longer a GtkToggleButton), via AWG_CHECK_{GET,SET}_ACTIVE
- Disconnect widget signal handlers when the editor is disposed: the
  host drops the editor before tearing the page down, and GTK4 then
  emits row-selected on the peer list, which crashed
  gnome-control-center
- Log and return UI load failures instead of g_return_val_if_reached
- Drop the GTK3-only type-hint property from the GTK3 dialog

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
